      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `arrayIsCached` returns `false` when the cached `CachedArray` was built from a different-sized array than the key array (size mismatch: key array has 7 elements, but `CachedArray.lastKnownSize` is 4). Let me write a more understandable version.Now let me compile-check it.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version uses descriptive variable names (`sevenElementArray`, `fourElementArray`, `cachedArrayForFour`, `isCached`) and adds inline comments explaining the deliberate size-mismatch setup and why `arrayIsCached` must return `false`."
